# Python A2A agents (LangGraph)

- Full type hints on public functions, graph state, node I/O, tools, and clients.
- Define graph state explicitly (Pydantic or `TypedDict`). Keep nodes small, deterministic, and testable.
- Separate prompt construction, model invocation, tool execution, validation, and state transitions.
- Validate node outputs and all inbound/outbound agent messages with schemas. Treat other agents as untrusted.
- Allowlist tools per agent. Sensitive/destructive tools require authorization, auditability, and (by default) human approval.
- Prevent prompt injection from overriding system/security/authorization instructions; separate instructions from data.
- Add timeouts and max-iteration guards. Avoid broad `except Exception` and hidden global mutable state.
- Never put secrets or full PII in prompts, traces, or Langfuse-visible fields; redact before emitting.

For deeper guidance load:
`resources/python-langgraph-agents.md`, `resources/security-by-design.md`,
`resources/observability-langfuse.md`.
